# Testing Rules

## Stack

- Unit: Vitest
- Component (web): Testing Library
- Component (native): React Native Testing Library
- Web E2E: Playwright
- Shared helpers: `packages/testing` / `tooling/vitest` (when created)

## Ownership

- Packages own their unit/component tests.
- Apps own integration + E2E tests.
- Do not skip validation for the active phase.

## Minimum bar (when implementation phases begin)

- New logic in `utils` / `validation` / `state` ships with unit tests.
- New `ui-*` components ship with at least a render/interaction test.
- App shells ship with a smoke E2E (web) or render test (native).

## Agent rules

- Prefer colocated `*.test.ts(x)` next to the unit under test unless a package convention differs.
- Keep tests deterministic; no flaky sleeps or network without mocks.
- Never mark a phase `COMPLETED` unless its declared quality gates pass.

See `docs/architecture/testing.md`.
